    <meta name='description' content='The Z13.physics ball from the X3D export conformance suite. Blender simulated a rigid-body drop and the exporter baked it into a PositionInterpolator with 49 keys; the keyValues here are those keys, unchanged (x and z fixed, only the height varies). The gold dots mark every key. The ball lands at key 25 and stays: the baked motion is faithful, and the simulation it came from never bounced. No Script.'/>
